preConditionHook:
// THE FOLLOW-THROUGH BAR EXTENDS MANY TICKS, NOT A FEW. This bar's high is at
// least extensionTicks above the PRIOR bar's high (mirrored: its low that far
// below the prior low). V15-08's whole content is the SIZE of the extension --
// "a few ticks beyond means a failed breakout, many ticks means a strong trend
// bar" -- so the margin is the input to optimize; Brooks gives no number and 4
// is the miner's reading.
//
// Not LaggedHigherHigh, which asks only that a higher high happened and has no
// margin input; at extensionTicks = 1 the two nearly coincide on a tick grid.
//
// DISTINCT FROM BreakoutClearsPriorExtremeByMargin, which clears the extreme of
// a whole lookback window rather than one bar: that rule at lookback = 1 is this
// rule, and only there. Both are authored, since a 20-bar level and the bar next
// door are different events on every bar but a breakout's first.
//
// The rule reads only highs, so it is knowable before the bar closes -- which
// matches the book's framing of judging the follow-through bar in progress.
//
// The tick is written division-first, mirroring EL's MinMove / PriceScale, and
// read once per bar into a local since both are per-symbol constants. Every
// scratch value is a localVariables entry, never a hook-scope declaration, so
// the hooks survive a double placement. Deepest bar touched: 1.
tickSize = ctx.MinMove() / ctx.PriceScale();
